%%label IV. Finale: Allegro giocoso
%%note A major, a rondo in 6/8 that keeps tipping into 3/4. The refrain is the motto as a dance; the first episode sets the slow movement's song over plucked strings; the second is a fugato in F sharp minor; the coda combines song and dance and recalls the first movement's curtain-raiser.
X:1
T:Bernstein’s Missing Quartet
T:IV. Finale: Allegro giocoso
C:Lor, in the manner of Leonard Bernstein
M:6/8
L:1/8
Q:"Allegro giocoso" 3/8=100
%%score [1 | 2 | 3 | 4]
V:1 clef=treble name="Vl. I"
V:2 clef=treble name="Vl. II"
V:3 clef=alto name="Vla."
V:4 clef=bass name="Vc."
K:A
V:1
